'''Xanthosoma robustum''', also known as Elephant Ear,<ref>{{Cite web |title=elephant ear (Xanthosoma robustum) |url=https://www.inaturalist.org/taxa/284200-Xanthosoma-robustum |access-date=2025-09-20 |website=iNaturalist |language=en}}</ref> is a robust herbaceous plant native to [[Central Mexico]] and [[Central America]] that can grow up to 4 meters tall.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Xanthosoma robustum Schott {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:89369-1 |access-date=2025-09-20 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Plant Atlas |url=https://florida.plantatlas.usf.edu/genus/1303 |access-date=2025-09-20 |website=florida.plantatlas.usf.edu}}</ref> It's an important plant with uses in medicine, environmental applications, and as a food source. This species has large, waxy, green leaves that can grow over a meter long. The plant also produces distinct inflorescences with a white to yellowish-green spathe and a pale yellow to ochre spadix.

